Upon completion of this course, students should be able to:
• Understand the fundamental principles of property returns, the key concepts and the important relations underlying commercial real estate and property cashflows
• Understand the nature of return and risk quantification and characteristics of property investment appraisals;
• Understand financial modelling techniques and how to apply them to evaluate investment returns;
• Develop robust, fully integrated financial forecasting models, which include sensitivity analysis and data tables
• Critically analyze and evaluate investment appraisals;
• Understand and apply the knowledge of property investment analysis skills to real world practices and deliver excellent services to potential clients, making informed investment decisions;
• Develop creative thinking, self-managed ability, team work spirit, analytical and communicative skills through case studies and project presentations.

